label chapter_3_1:
    scene bg JP RESTAURANT

    nvl clear

    n "I tried poking at my plate full of fresh sashimi."

    n "I wanted to eat it, but there was a rotten stench wafting through the area, like a fish just died. Well, considering one's remains were in front of me, that was true, but this smelt like a natural death. Like somebody let a different fish die on the kitchen floor and didn't clean it up. I wished that they checked the health and safety inspection papers up front before we came inside. The stench wouldn't leave, and honestly, it was ruining my appetite."

    nvl clear

    n "I picked up a slice of salmon. White pieces of sinew littered it. I was about to retch from the smell around me, but I put it carefully in my mouth. I chewed. I kept chewing, but I couldn't mash the sashimi well in my mouth even though it was already so soft, but I kept chewing. I was about to spit it out. I kept chewing, and chewing, and chewing,"

    nvl clear

    son "\"....?\""

    son "\".....\""

    son "\"Eugh.\""

    nvl clear

    n "On the plate, I spat out a piece of fish bone. For a brief moment I thought of a scenario where if I swallowed the fish bone, I would die a horrible death, by way of it piercing a hole into my throat and letting me internally bleed out. The sinew looked like a foreign growth. I tried looking at the other food, but they were all equally unappetizing. Mouths chewing in sync. My grandfather looked like an animal because of the way his jaw would move up and down, trying to grind food up. My mother then looked like a hamster, because of how little she'd eat per piece, like as if the food was not worth eating at all. My father didn't even bother. He only desired to smoke. He would open his mobile phone then and again. I bet he's anticipating a text. Maybe from his work―another woman, or perhaps it could even be from my teachers. Because I didn't want to look at the food, I continued scanning the crowd from left-to-right. All of them were equally disgusting. They appeared to be pigs feasting in a small barn."

    return
